# The .ch10 fixtures are large and mostly gitignored, EXCEPT the small
# (<100 MB) committed CI fixtures below, which CI needs. The full-size
# variants (e.g. the full PRN and Safran recordings) stay local-only, read by the
# release benchmark and the soak. "data/test files/" is the canonical fixture
# folder - everything else directly under data/ (stray exports, scratch csv/png,
# one-off recordings) is ignored outright, and within test files/ itself only the
# five small recordings below are tracked, with the third-party CSV log (a 1.3 MB text file, not a recording);
# the multi-GB "full" siblings next to them stay local-only on purpose.
data/*
!data/test files/
data/test files/*
!data/test files/agc_nzl_rasa_testfile.ch10
!data/test files/agc_rnrz-l_trc_testfile.ch10
!data/test files/prn_testfile, sample.ch10
!data/test files/safran_testfile, sample.ch10
# Real step-calibration recording (6.8 MB) with receivers far out of alignment -
# pins the calibration-import resilience fixes against the file that exposed them.
!data/test files/step_cal, example.ch10
# A log written by another application, the reference for US10.0 (importing a third-party CSV): ISO 8601 times, one row
# a polarization, 30 streams. Small enough to commit, and CI reads it.
!data/test files/av_snr_log.csv

# Output of the Qt-era test runner (QtTest's results*.txt): nothing writes here any more, so a leftover folder is
# not a change to commit.
output/
